meta {
  name: me update (edit the profile)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{bff_url}}/api/me
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "handle": "alice_prime",
    "preferred_currency": "EUR",
    "landing_page": "collection"
  }
}

docs {
  Cookie-authenticated profile edit through the gateway: expect 200
  with the refreshed Me projection, and the bff drops its brief
  /api/me cache so the next "me" shows the change immediately. The
  user service's validation problems relay verbatim (400 invalid_body
  naming the field, 409 handle_taken when another account owns the
  folded key, 429 handle_cooldown on a repeat change inside the
  cooldown window). Logins never overwrite this: provider claims fill
  the profile only when the account is first created. preferred_currency
  drives the SPA's display conversion; pattern ^[A-Z]{3}$, validated by
  the user service.
}
